# First-party SHACL Rules case: a RUN-ONCE rule inside a later stratum.
#
# SPARQL 1.2 RL §4.4 splits every stratification layer into (once, general).
# `once` holds the rules that produce blank nodes in the rule head; each is
# evaluated EXACTLY ONCE at the start of its layer. `general` holds the rest,
# iterated to fixpoint.
#
#   sh:order 0 — a general sh:TripleRule typing every ex:Employee as an ex:Person.
#   sh:order 1 — a run-once sh:SPARQLRule whose CONSTRUCT template carries a blank
#                node, minting one address resource per ex:Person focus node.
#
# The run-once rule starts its OWN layer, not the run. Because the order-0 layer
# is materialized first, `ex:alice rdf:type ex:Person` already holds when the
# order-1 layer resolves its sh:targetClass focus nodes, so the mint fires for
# ex:alice. A scheduler that hoisted every run-once rule to the start of the whole
# run would find no ex:Person at all and derive nothing here.
#
# Exactly ONE address blank is minted per focus node: the rule is not re-evaluated
# after its single firing.

@prefix ex:  <http://example.org/ns#> .
@prefix rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix sh:  <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#> .

ex:alice rdf:type ex:Employee .

ex:TypeRule
  rdf:type sh:NodeShape ;
  sh:targetClass ex:Employee ;
  sh:rule [
      rdf:type sh:TripleRule ;
      sh:order 0 ;
      sh:subject sh:this ;
      sh:predicate rdf:type ;
      sh:object ex:Person ] .

ex:AddrRule
  rdf:type sh:NodeShape ;
  sh:targetClass ex:Person ;
  sh:rule [
      rdf:type sh:SPARQLRule ;
      sh:order 1 ;
      sh:construct """CONSTRUCT { $this ex:addr _:a . _:a ex:city ex:Metropolis . }
                      WHERE { $this a ex:Person }""" ] .
